# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every working tree, on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says. Prettier (endOfLine: lf), `pnpm inventory` and the byte-for-byte checks
# below all expect LF; a CRLF checkout fails `pnpm format:check` and `pnpm tecton:check`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact files: never convert line endings. Each one is checked against a sha256 or
# compared with a fresh generator run, so a converted checkout fails the check.
#   vendored Tecton artifacts, hashed in vendor/<version>/manifest.json (`pnpm tecton:check`)
packages/tecton-adapter/vendor/** -text
#   Tecton adapter `emit` output, hashed in GENERATED.json and compared with a fresh emit
packages/ui/src/styles/tecton/generated/** -text
packages/ui/assets/tecton/** -text
#   docs-sync output, hashed in tooling/docs-sync/sync-lock.json (`pnpm docs:sync --check`)
apps/docs/src/mui-docs/generated/** -text

# Binary assets: no conversion, no textual diff or merge.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
